---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Contact from "../components/Contact.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Draigon Idle and draigonidle.com collect about you. The short version: the game collects nothing."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>Last updated: {site.legalUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="container prose">
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>The short version.</strong> The game doesn't collect anything about
          you. It has no accounts, no ads, no analytics and no tracking, and your save
          stays on your phone. This site only learns your email address if you sign up
          for the newsletter.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Who this is from</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is made by {site.person}, an independent developer publishing as
        {site.studio}. "We" and "us" on this page mean {site.person}. This policy
        covers the {site.name} app for iPhone and the website at draigonidle.com.
      </p>

      <h2>The game</h2>
      <h3>What it stores</h3>
      <p>
        Your progress is saved in a file on your device. It isn't sent to us or to
        anyone else, and we can't see it. Because it's part of the app's data, it may
        be included in your own device backups if you've turned those on with Apple.
        Deleting the app deletes the save.
      </p>

      <h3>What it doesn't do</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>No account, sign-in or profile.</li>
        <li>No advertising and no advertising identifiers.</li>
        <li>No analytics or tracking software.</li>
        <li>No access to your contacts, photos, location, camera or microphone.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Notifications</h3>
      <p>
        If you allow them, the game reminds you when a party is home, a cart has
        arrived and so on. These are scheduled on your device by the game itself. No
        server is involved, and you can turn each kind off in the game's Settings or
        all of them in your phone's Settings.
      </p>

      <h3>The purchase</h3>
      <p>
        The game has one optional purchase, which opens the full game. Apple handles
        the payment. We never see your name, card or billing details. The game is only
        told whether your Apple account owns the purchase, and it keeps that answer in
        your save. Apple's handling of your payment is covered by
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" rel="noopener">Apple's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>The beta (TestFlight)</h3>
      <p>
        If you test the game through Apple's TestFlight, Apple passes on what you
        choose to send us: written feedback, screenshots and crash reports, along with
        basic details such as your device model and iOS version. If you were invited by
        email, we have the address the invitation went to. We use these only to fix the
        game and to reach you about the beta, and we delete tester details when the
        beta ends or when you ask.
      </p>

      <h3>What Apple shows us</h3>
      <p>
        Apple gives every developer sales and download totals, and usage and crash
        figures from people who have agreed to share them with developers. These are
        grouped together and don't identify you.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is served by Cloudflare. Like any web host,
          Cloudflare processes your IP address and browser details to deliver pages and
          to keep the site secure. See
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Newsletter.</strong> If you sign up, your email address is stored by
          our email provider, Kit. We use it only to send news about {site.name}. Every
          email has an unsubscribe link. The sign-up form is loaded from Kit's servers,
          so Kit receives the usual details of that request. See
          <a href="https://kit.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Kit's privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No ads or trackers.</strong> We don't run advertising, and we don't set
          cookies to follow you between sites.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Links.</strong> Discord, X, Reddit and the App Store are run by other
          companies and follow their own policies.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We don't sell personal information and we don't share it for advertising. The
        only companies involved are the ones named above (Apple, Cloudflare and Kit),
        each for the job described.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} isn't directed at children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect
        personal information from them. If you believe a child has given us an email
        address, tell us and we'll delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To erase your game data, delete the app.</li>
        <li>To leave the newsletter, use the link in any email.</li>
        <li>
          To see, correct or delete anything we hold about you (a newsletter address or
          beta details), ask us. Depending on where you live, the law may give you
          further rights over your personal information, and we'll honour them.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If the game or the site starts handling information differently, this page will
        change first and the date at the top will be updated.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about privacy: reach us at <Contact />.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
